Issue #4395: PlanGraph.addTask permits creating cyclic graphs by omitting cycle detection validation

## Description

In `packages/franken-planner/src/core/dag.ts`, `PlanGraph` is intended to maintain an immutable Directed Acyclic Graph (DAG) invariant. Methods like `PlanGraph.fromTasks` validate acyclicity using Kahn's algorithm (`_kahn()`) before constructing the graph.

However, `PlanGraph.prototype.addTask` adds a new task and edges directly without running cycle detection or topological sort validation:

```ts
addTask(task: Task, dependsOn: TaskId[] = task.dependsOn): PlanGraph {
  if (this._nodes.has(task.id)) {
    throw new DuplicateTaskError(task.id);
  }
  for (const depId of dependsOn) {
    if (!this._nodes.has(depId)) {
      throw new Error(`Dependency '${depId}' not found in graph`);
    }
  }
  const newNodes = new Map(this._nodes);
  newNodes.set(task.id, { ...task, dependsOn: [...dependsOn] });
  const newEdges = new Map(this._edges);
  newEdges.set(task.id, new Set(dependsOn));
  return new PlanGraph(newNodes, newEdges, this.version + 1, `task added: '${task.id}'`);
}
```

`addTask` only checks whether `depId` exists in `_nodes`, but does NOT verify that adding the dependency preserves acyclicity. Consequently, a caller can introduce cycle-forming edges into `PlanGraph` via `addTask()` without triggering an exception at mutation time. The invalid state persists silently in the `PlanGraph` instance until `topoSort()` is later called.

## Location
- `packages/franken-planner/src/core/dag.ts`, L260-L274

## Impact
Violates the core invariant of `PlanGraph` as a verified DAG container and defers cycle detection errors from graph construction time to execution time.


